          alt: "Breaking the route from faeces to mouth: faeces travel by fingers, flies, fluids, fields and food to the mouth. The barriers in order of how much they achieve: a latrine used by everyone in the house; hand-washing with soap at the two moments — after the toilet and before touching food; safe water from a protected source, covered storage and a ladle rather than a dipped cup; food covered and reheated thoroughly; refuse and standing water cleared. Numbers worth carrying: free chlorine residual 0.2 to 0.5 mg per litre routinely, 0.5 or above at the point of use during an outbreak; latrine sited well away from and downhill of any well. Why building latrines usually fails: a latrine a household did not ask for becomes a store room; community-led total sanitation works because the community decides and builds; the unit of change is the whole village.",
